      "section": "Section A",
      "marks": 1,
      "question": "If $a, b, c$ are in A.P. and $x, y, z$ are in G.P., then the value of $x^{b-c} y^{c-a} z^{a-b}$ is",
      "options": [
        "0",
        "1",
        "xyz",
        "$x^a y^b z^c$"
      ],
      "finalAnswer": "(b) 1",
      "solutionSteps": [
        "Let common difference of AP be $d$. $b-c = -d, c-a = 2d, a-b = -d$.",
        "Let GP be $x, xr, xr^2$.",
        "$x^{-d} (xr)^{2d} (xr^2)^{-d} = x^{-d+2d-2d} r^{2d-2d} = x^{-d} r^0$. Wait.",
        "Correct: $b-c=-d, c-a=2d, a-b=-d$.",
        "$x^{-d} (xr)^{2d} (xr^2)^{-d} = x^{-d+2d-2d} r^{2d-2d} = x^{-d} r^0$. Something is wrong.",
        "Let's re-evaluate: $b-c = -d$. $c-a = 2d$. $a-b = -d$.",
        "$x^{b-c} y^{c-a} z^{a-b} = x^{-d} (xr)^{2d} (xr^2)^{-d} = x^{-d+2d-2d} r^{2d-2d}$.",
        "Wait, $x^{-d} x^{2d} x^{-2d}$? No. $x^{-d} x^{2d} x^{-d} = x^0 = 1$. $r^{2d} r^{-2d} = r^0 = 1$. Result is 1."
      ]
    },
